Usage: mkfifo [OPTION]... NAME...

Create named pipes (FIFOs) with the given NAMEs.

Windows has no filesystem FIFO node type, so WinuxCmd emulates one with
an on-disk marker file. WinuxCmd commands opening the marker for
reading or writing are bridged to a Windows named pipe with blocking
POSIX open() semantics; other tools see a small marker file.

OPTIONS:
  -m, --mode ARG          set file permission bits
  -Z, --security-context  set the SELinux security context to default type
      --context           set the SELinux security context
      --help              display this help and exit
  -V, --version           output version information and exit

EXIT STATUS:
  0  if OK,
  1  if minor problems,
  2  if serious trouble.

WinuxCmd is a Windows implementation of GNU CoreUtils for Linux-Windows developers and AI coding assistants.
